l__0OZLp" data-qd-rendered-description=3D"" data-track-load=3D"description_=
content"><p>Given an array of integers <code>nums</code> containing&nbsp;<c=
ode>n + 1</code> integers where each integer is in the range <code>[1, n]</=
code> inclusive.</p>

<p>There is only <strong>one repeated number</strong> in <code>nums</code>,=
 return <em>this&nbsp;repeated&nbsp;number</em>.</p>

<p>You must solve the problem <strong>without</strong> modifying the array =
<code>nums</code>&nbsp;and using only constant extra space.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums =3D [1,3,4,2,2]
<strong>Output:</strong> 2
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums =3D [3,1,3,4,2]
<strong>Output:</strong> 3
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 3:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> nums =3D [3,3,3,3,3]
<strong>Output:</strong> 3</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D n &lt;=3D 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>
	<li><code>nums.length =3D=3D n + 1</code></li>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D nums[i] &lt;=3D n</code></li>
	<li>All the integers in <code>nums</code> appear only <strong>once</strong=
> except for <strong>precisely one integer</strong> which appears <strong>t=
wo or more</strong> times.</li>
</ul>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><b>Follow up:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>How can we prove that at least one duplicate number must exist in <cod=
e>nums</code>?</li>
	<li>Can you solve the problem in linear runtime complexity?</li>
</ul>
